    "summary": "Epic Other One > Eyes jam, tight three‑set flow with sunshine",
    "blurb": "Features a monster Other One → Eyes of the World sequence and a radiant Here Comes Sunshine. The band delivers crisp playing throughout the three‑set show, highlighted by strong Jerry leads and Phil’s bomb‑dropping bass.",
    "review": "May 13, 1973 finds the Dead at the Des Moines State Fairgrounds in top form, rolling through three sets that balance tight songcraft with soaring improvisation. The first set builds momentum with bright renditions of classics like Here Comes Sunshine and Playing In The Band, while the second set keeps the groove steady. The third set is where the night truly shines: after a spirited stretch of Truckin' and a seamless Drums segue, the band launches into an expansive Other One that morphs effortlessly into Eyes Of The World, showcasing Jerry’s newly‑found Wolf guitar tone and Phil’s cello‑like bass runs. The set closes with a luminous China Doll that glows over the crowd before a satisfying Casey Jones encore. Across all available tapes the performance is consistently high‑energy, making this May outing one of the standout outdoor shows of ’73.",
